      "column_1based": 269,
      "literal_call": "\\sotp",
      "arguments": 0,
      "native_aid_active_line": "Finally we show that a finite $3$-generic metric space is determined by $\\widetilde{\\mathcal{S}}_1, \\widetilde{\\mathcal{S}}_\\triangle$ and $\\mathcal{S}_\\sotp$. Suppose we have the data of $\\widetilde{\\mathcal{S}}_1, \\widetilde{\\mathcal{S}}_\\triangle$ and $\\mathcal{S}_\\sotp$. Choose a triangle and an edge of it. "
